# The revision of libviprs/acadrust (the fork, never hakanaktt/acadrust) that
# this suite's second emitter is built and tested against.
#
# `Cargo.toml` depends on it as `{ path = "../acadrust", optional = true }`
# behind the `acadrust` feature, so CI lays a checkout down beside this one, and
# this file says which commit it gets. It is the same mechanism and the same
# rules as COUNTERPART_REV, from the same script (`tools/counterpart.sh`, with
# `COUNTERPART_NAME=acadrust`): one committed sha, fetched as a sha, verified
# after checkout, no branch name, no repository variable, no fallback.
#
# The merged-only rule, with reachability: this may only name a commit that
# `git merge-base --is-ancestor` finds on the fork's `main`. A commit that
# shares no history with `main` (a rewrite of main from the root) and a commit
# on a branch that has not merged are both refused, on every ref.
#
# The fork and not upstream, because upstream is at 0.6.4 against the fork's
# 0.5.5 and moves its entity API in ordinary commits. The emitter is written
# against the fork, so a fork sync and a pin bump are one change.
#
# The first line below that is neither blank nor a comment is the pin, and it is
# the whole line. A sha written inside one of these comments is prose.
#
# To bump it: put a libviprs/acadrust `main` commit here, run the suite with the
# `acadrust` feature against a sibling checkout at that commit, and say below
# what moved.
